> Work, optional history and explicit limits

fermat_factor retains its compiled one-argument signature and five-million
square-test default. fermat_factor_work returns the same solver's counts
without optional history. fermat_factor_trace captures one whole FermatStep
per actual odd square test, in the same pass. All inputs require n≥2 and
a positive trial budget; the historical meaningless returns for zero and
one are now rejected. Even fast paths validate the controls too.

C=captured_entries=rows.size() counts whole records. The trace admits each
record before its square/root work. Its default one-million-record quota
is independent of the five-million-test budget. A zero max_entries disables
only that quota; it does not disable the trial budget. A failed admission
or allocation throws without returning a partial trace. This is a count
of owned records, excluding scalar metadata, vector capacity, allocators
and runtime storage, so it is not a peak-memory guarantee.

For this fixed uint64/uint128 representation, each root uses at most 63
division comparisons. Ordinary/work calls take O(T) such fixed-word work
and constant auxiliary storage; a successful trace takes O(T) records.
With arbitrary-size integers, root and multiplication costs depend on the
bit length and cannot be folded into a unit-cost claim. In the prime case,
reaching (n+1)/2 takes order n tests, exponential in input bit length.
The budget bounds actual work, while the optional quota bounds captured
records. Factor-gap plots are measured work on selected inputs, not timing
benchmarks or a claim that this beats general factorization methods.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fermat_capture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory_extra.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <cstdint>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  bool quota=false;try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_factor_trace(5959,3,2);}catch(const std::length_error&){quota=true;}const auto admitted=dm::algorithms::fermat_factor_trace(5959,3,3);const auto noquota=dm::algorithms::fermat_factor_trace(5959,3,0);const auto work=dm::algorithms::fermat_factor_work(5959,3);
  std::print("Quota controls: two-record quota rejects third trial {}; exact quota captures {}; disabled quota captures {}; ordinary work tests {}.\n",quota,admitted.captured_entries,noquota.captured_entries,work.trials);
  auto edited=admitted;const auto owned=edited;edited.rows.front().a=0;std::print("Owned copy: retained first a {}; edited first a {}; stored outcome factor {}.\n",owned.rows.front().a,edited.rows.front().a,edited.outcome.returned_factor);
  int invalid=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_factor(0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_factor_trace(1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::fermat_factor_work(10,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}std::print("Invalid zero/one/zero-budget controls rejected {}/3.\n",invalid);
  std::print("\n| actual-history family | odd n | first factor | actual tests | captured records |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB>colours{{37,99,235},{220,38,38},{22,163,74}};const std::vector<std::string>names{"Odd squares","p=101, q=1009","Prime 9973"};for(int family=0;family<3;++family){std::vector<double>x,y;for(std::uint64_t n:family==0?std::vector<std::uint64_t>{9,49,121}:family==1?std::vector<std::uint64_t>{101ULL*1009}:std::vector<std::uint64_t>{9973}){const auto t=dm::algorithms::fermat_factor_trace(n,5000,5000);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",names[family],n,t.outcome.returned_factor,t.outcome.trials,t.captured_entries);x.push_back(t.outcome.trials);y.push_back(t.captured_entries);}plot.points(x,y,names[family],colours[family],7);}plot.line({1,5000},{1,5000},"C = T",{100,116,139},1).title("Optional history stores one record per actual odd test").x_label("Actual square tests T").y_label("Captured whole records C").size(1100,560).save_svg("build/fermat_capture.svg");if(!quota||invalid!=3||owned.rows.front().a!=78)throw std::runtime_error("capture controls failed");
}
